 "generalAt": [30,14],
 "briefing": "Day one hundred. They did not wait for nightfall; there is none up here.\n\nHesk's fleet is at the gates: Directorate hulls, cartel guns bought with Ninefold money, and machines Eden sold to pay for its air. The north is already full of them. More will come round the west, through the old breach in the east, and from the dark.\n\nThe Command Centre is the heart of Eden. If it falls, so does the colony. The lift shafts are the way in for anything small; the hull guns stand in them.\n\nHold until they break. There is no paying these people off.",
 "strategy": [
  "Keep the Command Centre ringed: the bulkheads beside it have one door each, at row 16.",
  "Waves: the west on turn 3, the east breach on turn 5, the General's old machines from the north on turn 7, and a last push from three sides on turn 10.",
  "Ships cannot cross the hull: only the dock mouth and the lift shafts lead inside for them. Craft and mecha can climb anywhere."
 ],
 "transmission": "You read my name to the whole sky, General. Now read this: I am coming home to Eden."
}
